<Base title="About GuideHollow" description="GuideHollow is an independent, hands-on English resource offering verifiable AI guides, browser-based audit workbenches, and reproducible practice datasets." breadcrumbs={[{name:'About',url:'/about/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ about</p><h1>A clearer path<br />through AI.</h1><p>Practical workflows, inspectable examples, and free browser tools designed so readers can verify every step themselves.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Why GuideHollow exists</h2><p>Most AI advice stops at clever one-line prompts and skips the hard part: checking whether the answer actually fits your source notes, arithmetic, privacy rules, or workflow constraints. A polished paragraph can still drop a timestamp boundary, silently accept an unapproved requirement, or invent a citation.</p><p>GuideHollow is built to close that gap in plain English. Every guide tackles one concrete, everyday problem—summarizing long documents without losing key obligations, validating spreadsheet totals, checking chart descriptions against source CSVs, or cleaning Unicode text—and pairs step-by-step instructions with testable inputs and browser utilities.</p><h2>What makes GuideHollow different</h2><p>Rather than publishing generic summaries that readers cannot test, we design reproducible exercises backed by automated quality checks and primary product documentation:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Resource type</th><th>How you can use it</th><th>Verification built in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Practical Guides (38 published)</td><td>Step-by-step workflows with exact stop conditions and common failure modes</td><td>Primary documentation references and worked boundary cases</td></tr><tr><td>Free Browser Tools (4 utilities)</td><td>Format structured prompts, audit weighted CSV math, review claims, and export TSV records locally</td><td>Runs 100% client-side with automated browser tests and zero data upload</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence Library</td><td>Download original PDF OCR pairs, CSV sales datasets, TSV audits, and prompt test sheets</td><td>Every fixture is validated deterministically against reference scripts in CI</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Who publishes and maintains GuideHollow</h2><p>GuideHollow is independently published and engineered by <a href="https://github.com/emfls">emfls</a> as an open-source educational library under the <strong>GuideHollow Editorial</strong> imprint. Rather than concealing revisions behind unattributed pages, our entire article collection, browser utilities, downloadable test fixtures, and 80+ automated test suites live openly in the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">GuideHollow public repository</a>.</p><h2>Our editorial and technical quality process</h2><p>Every guide published on GuideHollow goes through structured research against official documentation, hands-on verification with inspectable source inputs, and automated build validation before reaching readers. We distinguish clearly between controlled classroom fixtures (explicitly labeled as invented teaching inputs), directly observed runs of our browser tools, and documented primary vendor policies. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> details how we verify citations, track dates, and correct mistakes.</p><h2>See the work, not just the claims</h2><p>Readers never have to take any claim on faith. You can download our <a href="/examples/weighted-price-sample.csv">eight-row sales CSV fixture</a>, compute channel-level totals directly inside the <a href="/tools/weighted-price-checker/">Weighted Average Audit Workbench</a>, and compare every figure step-by-step in our <a href="/guides/verify-ai-weighted-average-price-spreadsheet/">spreadsheet verification walkthrough</a>. Our <a href="/evidence/">Evidence Library</a> gathers all original CSV, TSV, PDF, and XLSX practice assets alongside automated test coverage and documented edge cases.</p><h2>Measured operational checks on our live site</h2><p>We verify GuideHollow's own behavior with the same standard we teach. For instance, our <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow/actions/runs/41540809663">November 2, 2026 GitHub Pages deployment run</a> executed the public <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow/blob/main/scripts/verify-public-readiness.mjs">readiness checker</a> across 16 selected live routes and confirmed every expected HTTP 200 route plus an intentional HTTP 404 check on the first pass. Publishing those automated runs provides concrete first-party deployment verification; it is not a visitor study, a live AI model benchmark, or a Google AdSense approval status. Our <a href="/guides/what-is-generative-ai/">beginner guide</a> walks through how to read logs and boundaries carefully without overclaiming.</p><h2>Who reviews, tests, and corrects articles</h2><p>Each publication is reviewed by the GuideHollow maintainer through the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">public repository workflow</a>, supported by automated link integrity, metadata consistency, accessibility, and calculation unit tests on every push. Every guide carries a clear review scope: for example, our <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow/blob/main/docs/editorial-fact-check-2026-11-01.md">November 1 audit register</a> documents a <strong>historical snapshot of 31 articles</strong>, while newer interactive exercises such as our <a href="/ai-tools/notebooklm-source-checked-study-guide/">NotebookLM source-checking guide</a> include fresh downloadable sources and reference answer keys.</p><h2>Four free browser utilities built for everyday judgment</h2><ul><li>Four free browser tools for drafting a structured prompt, reviewing an AI answer, auditing weighted averages, and building a locally exported source-claim record.</li><li>Zero sign-up, zero tracking analytics, and zero backend uploads—your inputs remain inside your own browser tab.</li><li>Transparent limitations on every tool page so you always know what a browser check verifies and what requires primary-source human judgment.</li></ul><h2>How to report an error or suggest a guide</h2><p>If you spot an outdated software label, an accessibility defect, or an unclear verification rule, send the exact URL and reference link via our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Every confirmed correction updates both the article and its visible revision history. GuideHollow is completely free to read and offers no paid consulting, paid placements, or hidden affiliate endorsements.</p><h2>Start somewhere useful</h2><p>Explore <a href="/guides/what-is-generative-ai/">how generative AI fits real tasks</a>, practice <a href="/prompts/how-to-write-better-ai-prompts/">writing bounded prompts</a>, or test an example directly in the <a href="/tools/ai-prompt-builder/">AI Prompt Builder</a>.</p></article>
</Base>
